# Stitch design source

Project: **Crease Cricket Team Management**  
ID: `projects/5487252279778690236`  
Design system: **Modern Cricket Club**  
Asset: `assets/11807811405223687109`

Supersedes Athletic Precision / Roboto Flex. Do not revert to the old DS.

## When implementing or updating UI

1. Pull screens / design system via Stitch MCP first.
2. Do not copy generated HTML — rebuild with reusable React components.
3. Keep tokens in sync: `src/styles/globals.css` **and** `src/constants/design-tokens.ts`.
4. Prefer editing shared tokens/components over per-screen one-off styles.

## Typography

| Role | Face | Via |
|---|---|---|
| Headlines, match titles, dates, fees, counts, scores | **Barlow Condensed** | `font-heading` + `Display` / `Title` / `Heading` / `typography.statValue` |
| Body, labels, forms, nav | **Manrope** | `--font-sans` / `Body` / `LabelText` |

Never use Inter or Roboto as brand voice.

## Color (use sparingly)

| Token | Hex | Use |
|---|---|---|
| Canvas | `#F5F2E8` | Page background |
| Pitch green | `#0B5D2A` | Primary actions, brand |
| Clubhouse dark | `#082417` | Match tickets / fixture posters |
| Electric lime | `#C9F64B` | Selected / positive / key accent **only** |
| Urgency red | `#C83E35` | Unpaid, not playing, destructive, critical |

Do not paint every tertiary surface lime. Lime is reserved for selection and confirmation accents.

## Layout & chrome

- Touch targets ≥ 48px. Radius DEFAULT 8px (`ROUND_EIGHT`).
- Mobile bottom nav; desktop sidebar.
- Prefer tonal surfaces over borders/shadows.
- Prefer bottom sheets for create-tournament, add-player, confirm, pay.
- Avoid glassmorphism, generic gradients, nested cards, purple accents, decorative cricket clipart.

## Signature patterns

- **Match ticket** — dominant dark `#082417` surface for next/fixture (see `MatchTicket`).
- **SegmentedControl** — lime active state for Playing / Carpool / Warmup|Tournament / time.
- **Status rail** — compact metrics strip, not a card grid.
- **Admin quick actions** — secondary tonal chips; never compete with the next match.
